1
00:02:58,160 --> 00:02:59,640
Give me back my son.

2
00:03:01,880 --> 00:03:03,640
- You must die.
- I'm scared.

3
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:06,039
Kang is your son.

4
00:03:06,040 --> 00:03:07,360
My child.

5
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:10,999
His voice sounds familiar too.

6
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:14,760
But I can't remember where I heard it.

7
00:03:31,560 --> 00:03:35,680
I'm glad you finally know the truth.

8
00:03:41,400 --> 00:03:42,680
You bastard.

9
00:03:50,920 --> 00:03:53,320
Why aren't you begging for your life?

10
00:03:59,960 --> 00:04:01,480
Begging?

11
00:04:02,800 --> 00:04:04,280
I've been waiting for this moment.

12
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:08,840
Waiting for the chance
to pay with my life. Why would I beg?

13
00:04:13,040 --> 00:04:16,640
You think talking like this
is going to make me forgive you?

14
00:04:18,920 --> 00:04:20,040
I know.

15
00:04:20,920 --> 00:04:24,319
I know your spirit suffered

16
00:04:24,320 --> 00:04:26,880
in that coral forest beneath the sea.

17
00:04:27,840 --> 00:04:31,720
Me too. I've been suffering.

18
00:04:32,240 --> 00:04:35,599
Raising Kang all these years
felt like carrying hell inside my heart.

19
00:04:35,600 --> 00:04:36,760
Liar!

20
00:04:38,880 --> 00:04:42,160
Go ahead, Sarai. Kill me.

21
00:04:43,080 --> 00:04:44,440
I'm ready.

22
00:04:46,800 --> 00:04:48,760
I will kill you, you monster.

23
00:04:49,360 --> 00:04:51,120
Raising my son

24
00:04:52,080 --> 00:04:54,920
doesn't erase what you did to me.

25
00:05:12,040 --> 00:05:13,120
Why?

26
00:05:16,040 --> 00:05:17,840
Why didn't you kill me?

27
00:05:20,080 --> 00:05:21,960
If I kill you,

28
00:05:22,680 --> 00:05:25,120
that sin will follow me.

29
00:05:25,640 --> 00:05:27,719
A scumbag like you

30
00:05:27,720 --> 00:05:31,439
deserves to live
with the hell in your heart,

31
00:05:31,440 --> 00:05:34,920
so it can torment you
for the rest of your life, Thongdee.

32
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:17,680
Alright, we're finally home.

33
00:06:21,600 --> 00:06:24,360
Both mother and son are asleep.

34
00:06:26,200 --> 00:06:27,360
Sarai.

35
00:06:28,200 --> 00:06:29,240
Sarai.

36
00:06:32,160 --> 00:06:33,200
Sarai.

37
00:06:34,760 --> 00:06:35,960
Sarai?

38
00:06:37,800 --> 00:06:40,760
Sarai. Sarai.

39
00:06:41,360 --> 00:06:42,440
Sarai.

40
00:06:44,800 --> 00:06:45,920
Mr. Phum.

41
00:06:49,640 --> 00:06:51,080
You scared me.

42
00:06:52,920 --> 00:06:54,360
Are you alright?

43
00:06:56,520 --> 00:06:58,040
I must have fallen asleep.

44
00:07:01,840 --> 00:07:03,400
Should we wake him up?

45
00:07:05,320 --> 00:07:08,920
It's alright.
Just let him sleep. I'll carry him.

46
00:07:23,920 --> 00:07:25,680
Where did you go, Dad?

47
00:07:27,880 --> 00:07:29,840
Why did you turn off your phone?

48
00:07:30,520 --> 00:07:33,279
It's a long story. I'll tell you later.
I'll take Kang to bed first.

49
00:07:33,280 --> 00:07:35,720
It's alright. I'll do it.

50
00:07:51,960 --> 00:07:53,680
Kang is really my brother?

51
00:07:55,440 --> 00:07:56,760
Yes. There's no mistake.

52
00:08:01,840 --> 00:08:04,760
No wonder I felt attached to him
from the very beginning.

53
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:07,920
Me too.

54
00:08:08,680 --> 00:08:12,480
I only really understood
the meaning of a blood connection today.

55
00:08:16,840 --> 00:08:20,520
I'm happy for you, Sarai.
You finally found your son.

56
00:08:21,760 --> 00:08:23,680
Thank you, Mr. Narathon,

57
00:08:24,240 --> 00:08:26,720
for caring for Kang
and helping him all this time.

58
00:08:27,440 --> 00:08:28,480
It's nothing.

59
00:08:30,040 --> 00:08:31,280
And from now on,

60
00:08:32,360 --> 00:08:34,640
I'll take the best care of my brother.

61
00:08:41,760 --> 00:08:45,760
What are you going to do
about Sairung and Pong?

62
00:08:47,200 --> 00:08:50,840
At this point, we should let the police
handle it according to the law.

63
00:08:54,680 --> 00:08:56,920
Can we not report it yet?

64
00:08:58,000 --> 00:08:59,040
Why?

65
00:09:00,720 --> 00:09:04,760
Sairung knows
I'm inside Pakarang's body now.

66
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:08,519
If she gets arrested,
she'll definitely talk about it.

67
00:09:08,520 --> 00:09:11,400
Then the police will investigate Pakarang.

68
00:09:12,840 --> 00:09:14,840
I still want to use this body

69
00:09:15,720 --> 00:09:17,400
to be with my son for a while...

70
00:09:20,040 --> 00:09:21,600
even though I know

71
00:09:22,840 --> 00:09:24,840
it can't stay this way forever.

72
00:09:32,320 --> 00:09:34,000
I understand.

73
00:09:35,360 --> 00:09:36,800
I'll do as you ask.

74
00:09:37,640 --> 00:09:38,960
Even if Sairung

75
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:43,440
and Pong escape,
they can't escape the karma they created.

76
00:09:45,920 --> 00:09:47,560
Thank you, Mr. Phum.

77
00:09:50,600 --> 00:09:53,880
But I'm afraid
Sairung might come back to hurt Kang.

78
00:09:56,200 --> 00:09:58,120
After what happened to her,
she won't dare come back.

79
00:10:35,720 --> 00:10:38,440
- Why are you shouting?
- Ms. Sairung?

80
00:10:39,240 --> 00:10:40,960
Yes, it's me.

81
00:10:41,840 --> 00:10:42,800
You scared me.

82
00:10:43,520 --> 00:10:45,600
I thought that ghost
followed me all the way here.

83
00:10:51,840 --> 00:10:53,160
How did you get here?

84
00:10:54,160 --> 00:10:57,359
You still have the nerve to ask?
You ran off alone and left me there.

85
00:10:57,360 --> 00:10:59,880
I almost got killed by it.
I'm lucky I made it out alive.

86
00:11:01,040 --> 00:11:03,080
Your husband nearly beat me to death too.

87
00:11:06,480 --> 00:11:07,440
Most importantly,

88
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:09,560
he got the bag.

89
00:11:12,120 --> 00:11:13,280
Let's talk inside.

90
00:11:31,280 --> 00:11:32,800
What are you going to do now?

91
00:11:34,640 --> 00:11:35,839
I think

92
00:11:35,840 --> 00:11:38,559
we need to run as far away as possible.

93
00:11:38,560 --> 00:11:40,800
Your husband is definitely
going to call the police on us.

94
00:11:42,160 --> 00:11:45,200
I know. That's why I came to wait for you.

95
00:11:46,680 --> 00:11:49,840
I knew you'd come back here.

96
00:11:51,840 --> 00:11:53,360
So you have a plan?

97
00:11:55,200 --> 00:11:56,280
Yes.

98
00:12:00,920 --> 00:12:02,640
I'll take you somewhere with me.

99
00:12:03,160 --> 00:12:04,200
Where?

100
00:12:05,800 --> 00:12:06,880
Skull Island.

101
00:12:07,840 --> 00:12:08,800
What?

102
00:12:09,720 --> 00:12:11,800
You know there's gold there.

103
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:17,039
It was because of this gold
that I, Thongdee, and Sompong

104
00:12:17,040 --> 00:12:20,599
had to abduct Sarai
and force her to lead us to Skull Island.

105
00:12:20,600 --> 00:12:25,440
Then we accidentally killed her,
and everything spiraled into this mess.

106
00:12:26,400 --> 00:12:28,159
How dare you blame me?

107
00:12:28,160 --> 00:12:31,120
Back then, none of you knew the way.

108
00:12:32,200 --> 00:12:35,400
Sarai was a local, so I had to use her.

109
00:12:37,040 --> 00:12:41,039
If anyone's to blame,
it's you people, for ruining everything.

110
00:12:41,040 --> 00:12:44,800
Fine, fine.
There's no point blaming each other now.

111
00:12:46,840 --> 00:12:48,400
So are you going or not?

112
00:12:52,880 --> 00:12:54,200
But that place has ghosts.

113
00:12:55,360 --> 00:12:59,200
If there really were ghosts, how did
Narathon and the others make it back?

114
00:12:59,800 --> 00:13:01,880
Nothing happened to any of them.

115
00:13:04,480 --> 00:13:06,160
I've been thinking.

116
00:13:06,840 --> 00:13:10,840
Maybe they found the gold

117
00:13:11,480 --> 00:13:14,759
and made up the ghost story
to stop anyone from going to the island

118
00:13:14,760 --> 00:13:16,280
until they could move the gold away.

119
00:13:20,680 --> 00:13:21,600
So what do you say?

120
00:13:22,520 --> 00:13:26,240
If you won't go,
I'll hire someone else instead.

121
00:13:34,280 --> 00:13:35,840
Then we go 50-50.

122
00:13:36,800 --> 00:13:39,639
You agreed to 70-30 before.

123
00:13:39,640 --> 00:13:43,560
That was before.
The situation has changed.

124
00:13:54,080 --> 00:13:55,160
Fine.

125
00:14:20,640 --> 00:14:22,560
Na, may I come in?

126
00:14:24,520 --> 00:14:25,800
Come in, Mook.

127
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:37,760
Mom said
you're taking Da on a trip out of town.

128
00:14:38,480 --> 00:14:39,879
That's right.

129
00:14:39,880 --> 00:14:42,279
Da's been under a lot of stress lately,

130
00:14:42,280 --> 00:14:45,680
so I thought I'd take her to relax.
Hopefully it'll help her feel better.

131
00:14:48,120 --> 00:14:49,240
That's a good idea.

132
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:55,879
But I don't think
it'll be much of a vacation

133
00:14:55,880 --> 00:14:58,320
if you and Da are going to Skull Island.

134
00:15:00,960 --> 00:15:03,199
Uh, I...

135
00:15:03,200 --> 00:15:06,720
You're not very good at lying.
Don't even try.

136
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:12,000
You got me.

137
00:15:13,240 --> 00:15:15,080
Yes, Da and I are going to Skull Island.

138
00:15:16,160 --> 00:15:18,239
Even though you know how dangerous it is?

139
00:15:18,240 --> 00:15:19,440
Mook,

140
00:15:20,160 --> 00:15:23,680
last time, everything happened
because those ghosts wanted you.

141
00:15:24,640 --> 00:15:27,720
Da and I aren't their targets.
Don't worry.

142
00:15:29,120 --> 00:15:32,560
It's still dangerous. Please don't go.

143
00:15:36,480 --> 00:15:39,000
Mook, listen to me.

144
00:15:39,720 --> 00:15:41,759
If I disappeared,

145
00:15:41,760 --> 00:15:43,480
would you come looking for me?

146
00:15:44,520 --> 00:15:47,279
Of course. No matter where you were,

147
00:15:47,280 --> 00:15:49,800
I'd find you.

148
00:15:50,760 --> 00:15:51,680
Right.

149
00:15:52,200 --> 00:15:55,800
That's exactly how Da feels right now.
That's why I don't want to stop her.

150
00:15:56,560 --> 00:16:00,519
I'll take her there and let her see
for herself that Mr. Prawin isn't there,

151
00:16:00,520 --> 00:16:02,399
and then we'll come straight back.

152
00:16:02,400 --> 00:16:04,000
Don't worry.

153
00:16:06,240 --> 00:16:07,200
Alright, Mook?

154
00:16:08,400 --> 00:16:09,520
It'll be fine.

155
00:16:19,080 --> 00:16:21,200
If I were Mana,

156
00:16:22,160 --> 00:16:23,360
I'd probably do the same thing.

157
00:16:25,040 --> 00:16:27,880
I know. That's why I came to talk to you.

158
00:16:28,480 --> 00:16:30,040
I want to go with them.

159
00:16:31,280 --> 00:16:33,800
Hey. No.

160
00:16:34,400 --> 00:16:35,440
I won't let you go.

161
00:16:40,720 --> 00:16:42,599
But I'm worried about Na,

162
00:16:42,600 --> 00:16:44,879
just like Da is worried about Win.

163
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:46,880
Even though I know it's dangerous,

164
00:16:48,680 --> 00:16:51,800
how can I just sit here
and let him go alone?

165
00:16:53,880 --> 00:16:55,880
I know someone

166
00:16:57,840 --> 00:17:00,400
who might be able to advise us.

167
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:03,240
Who?

168
00:17:15,160 --> 00:17:16,240
Mr. Thongdee.

169
00:17:21,880 --> 00:17:23,000
Mr. Narathon.

170
00:17:24,160 --> 00:17:26,760
We'd like to ask for your advice.

171
00:17:29,520 --> 00:17:33,800
We want to go to Skull Island.

172
00:17:36,400 --> 00:17:37,520
Why?

173
00:17:39,080 --> 00:17:42,279
Da dreamed
that her brother was calling for help.

174
00:17:42,280 --> 00:17:44,319
She believes
something terrible has happened,

175
00:17:44,320 --> 00:17:47,240
and the place
she saw in her dream was Skull Island.

176
00:17:49,200 --> 00:17:50,199
Her brother?

177
00:17:50,200 --> 00:17:52,480
Yes, his name is Prawin.

178
00:17:56,440 --> 00:17:59,360
No!

179
00:18:02,800 --> 00:18:05,200
Stop creating more sins, Men.

180
00:18:16,640 --> 00:18:17,760
Do you have a picture of him?

181
00:18:19,840 --> 00:18:21,280
Just a second.

182
00:18:30,280 --> 00:18:31,720
‎Here.

183
00:18:42,840 --> 00:18:44,440
‎There's no use going there.

184
00:18:46,960 --> 00:18:47,800
‎Why?

185
00:18:50,160 --> 00:18:51,000
‎He's dead.

186
00:19:18,080 --> 00:19:21,440
‎Da, no one agreed to take us there.

187
00:19:31,800 --> 00:19:32,800
‎Yes, Mook?

188
00:19:36,840 --> 00:19:40,360
‎Okay. Let me ask Da first.

189
00:19:43,160 --> 00:19:44,400
Did Mook call?

190
00:19:45,080 --> 00:19:45,960
Yes.

191
00:19:47,040 --> 00:19:48,800
Mook and Mr. Narathon said

192
00:19:49,320 --> 00:19:51,760
they want us to meet them
at the beach house right now.

193
00:19:53,320 --> 00:19:56,760
Are Mook and Mr. Narathon coming with us?

194
00:19:58,920 --> 00:20:00,160
I don't know.

195
00:20:01,680 --> 00:20:05,320
Mook just said
she wants you to meet someone first.

196
00:20:17,400 --> 00:20:19,640
When did you leave the monkhood,
Venerable Sir?

197
00:20:20,960 --> 00:20:22,680
Just call me Thongdee.

198
00:20:27,720 --> 00:20:30,200
So, the person you wanted me to meet is...

199
00:20:31,800 --> 00:20:33,040
Mr. Thongdee?

200
00:20:35,160 --> 00:20:36,560
Yes.

201
00:20:37,600 --> 00:20:40,480
Mr. Thongdee has seen Win.

202
00:20:43,080 --> 00:20:45,040
Really? Where?

203
00:20:48,240 --> 00:20:49,880
On Skull Island.

204
00:20:52,280 --> 00:20:55,760
See? I told everyone.
Win really did go to Skull Island.

205
00:20:56,400 --> 00:20:59,200
Then let's hurry and go help him.

206
00:20:59,760 --> 00:21:02,200
Are you coming with us, Mr. Thongdee?

207
00:21:20,720 --> 00:21:23,080
Mr. Thongdee...

208
00:21:25,640 --> 00:21:27,160
already tried to save Prawin,

209
00:21:29,240 --> 00:21:30,360
but it was too late.

210
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:37,240
What do you mean?

211
00:21:46,440 --> 00:21:47,799
Da.

212
00:21:47,800 --> 00:21:49,760
Stay strong.

213
00:21:51,080 --> 00:21:54,880
Win is dead.

214
00:22:07,600 --> 00:22:08,760
It's not true, is it?

215
00:22:14,120 --> 00:22:15,160
That's not true.

216
00:22:16,720 --> 00:22:19,840
It can't be.

217
00:22:22,320 --> 00:22:25,200
Birth, aging, sickness, and death
are things everyone must face.

218
00:22:26,400 --> 00:22:29,360
We all have to accept them.

219
00:22:47,440 --> 00:22:50,160
Did that evil spirit kill Win?

220
00:23:00,880 --> 00:23:02,120
I understand now.

221
00:23:08,720 --> 00:23:11,120
It must have trapped Win's spirit there.

222
00:23:12,680 --> 00:23:15,800
That's why he kept trying to reach me.

223
00:23:25,600 --> 00:23:27,080
Is there any way

224
00:23:27,800 --> 00:23:30,880
to free my brother's spirit
from Skull Island?

225
00:23:32,920 --> 00:23:34,040
There is only one way.

226
00:23:38,120 --> 00:23:40,640
There must be a substitute.

227
00:23:56,960 --> 00:24:00,240
<i>The number you're trying
to reach can't be connected.</i>

228
00:24:02,880 --> 00:24:04,080
Why is her phone off?

229
00:24:07,360 --> 00:24:09,640
<i>The number you're trying
to reach can't be connected.</i>

230
00:24:12,720 --> 00:24:13,639
Thank you.

231
00:24:13,640 --> 00:24:15,640
I still can't reach Ms. Pat at all.

232
00:24:17,560 --> 00:24:19,000
Maybe she's busy.

233
00:24:19,520 --> 00:24:21,680
Once she sees your missed call,
she'll probably call you back.

234
00:24:30,920 --> 00:24:32,039
So, what do you think?

235
00:24:32,040 --> 00:24:34,039
Do you like these paintings?

236
00:24:34,040 --> 00:24:38,759
I do. They're all beautiful,
especially that island.

237
00:24:38,760 --> 00:24:40,280
What's the island called?

238
00:24:45,360 --> 00:24:46,520
This is Skull Island.

239
00:24:47,800 --> 00:24:49,719
That's a scary name.

240
00:24:49,720 --> 00:24:51,920
Does that mean
there are ghosts on the island?

241
00:24:52,560 --> 00:24:54,879
No. It's just a name.

242
00:24:54,880 --> 00:24:56,200
Well,

243
00:24:56,720 --> 00:24:59,159
since we can't reach Ms. Pat today anyway,

244
00:24:59,160 --> 00:25:01,040
how about I take you out
somewhere fun instead?

245
00:25:02,200 --> 00:25:05,120
Really? I love you so much, Dad.

246
00:25:05,840 --> 00:25:06,999
Where do you want to go?

247
00:25:07,000 --> 00:25:08,240
Anywhere, Dad.

248
00:25:09,200 --> 00:25:11,400
There are many places I want to take you.

249
00:25:20,400 --> 00:25:21,840
You're so fast.

250
00:25:26,360 --> 00:25:28,600
Let's stop here. I'm tired.

251
00:25:29,840 --> 00:25:32,279
I just realized I'm old.

252
00:25:32,280 --> 00:25:33,759
You're not old, Dad.

253
00:25:33,760 --> 00:25:35,519
- Really?
- Yes.

254
00:25:35,520 --> 00:25:38,440
- You're still young and very handsome.
- Oh.

255
00:25:39,040 --> 00:25:43,720
Such a sweet talker.
You really know what to say. Right, Sarai?

256
00:25:47,000 --> 00:25:49,839
- Are you thirsty, Kang?
- Yes.

257
00:25:49,840 --> 00:25:51,719
Go buy some water.
Get some for me and Mom too.

258
00:25:51,720 --> 00:25:52,880
Yes.

259
00:25:59,080 --> 00:26:00,199
Sarai,

260
00:26:00,200 --> 00:26:03,399
are you alright? You look worried.

261
00:26:03,400 --> 00:26:08,280
If something's bothering you, tell me.
Is it about Kang?

262
00:26:11,440 --> 00:26:12,800
No.

263
00:26:14,320 --> 00:26:16,000
I was thinking about my father.

264
00:26:17,120 --> 00:26:19,680
Should I take you to see him?

265
00:26:21,520 --> 00:26:23,080
He's dead.

266
00:26:27,120 --> 00:26:28,280
Then

267
00:26:29,080 --> 00:26:32,600
should I take you to make merit for him?

268
00:26:34,920 --> 00:26:36,760
He probably won't receive it.

269
00:26:37,760 --> 00:26:38,960
Why not?

270
00:26:41,280 --> 00:26:42,960
Because my father's spirit

271
00:26:44,040 --> 00:26:46,240
is trapped on Skull Island.

272
00:26:52,440 --> 00:26:56,080
Why can't our spirits leave this island?

273
00:26:59,240 --> 00:27:01,720
Knowing won't help you.

274
00:27:02,800 --> 00:27:04,720
I don't want to stay here.

275
00:27:05,360 --> 00:27:09,520
Please tell me. What do we
have to do to leave this island?

276
00:27:10,440 --> 00:27:11,800
Please tell me.

277
00:27:14,720 --> 00:27:17,320
There must be a substitute.

278
00:27:19,040 --> 00:27:20,600
A substitute?

279
00:27:33,680 --> 00:27:35,760
Where are we supposed
to find our substitutes?

280
00:27:37,000 --> 00:27:38,400
There are only ghosts on this island.

281
00:27:41,080 --> 00:27:42,479
Exactly.

282
00:27:42,480 --> 00:27:46,400
We can't even leave the island.

283
00:27:53,080 --> 00:27:55,440
Prawin, look.

284
00:28:03,120 --> 00:28:05,040
Our substitutes have arrived.

285
00:28:13,320 --> 00:28:16,440
How did your father
become that evil spirit's servant?

286
00:28:19,080 --> 00:28:20,840
I don't know.

287
00:28:24,240 --> 00:28:28,080
My father's spirit
must be suffering terribly.

288
00:28:29,120 --> 00:28:30,999
I pity him.

289
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:34,000
I want to help his spirit
be free and be reborn.

290
00:28:40,760 --> 00:28:41,840
Calm down.

291
00:28:42,920 --> 00:28:45,320
I'll try to find a way
to help your father.

292
00:28:47,760 --> 00:28:49,880
Thank you, Mr. Phum.

293
00:28:55,360 --> 00:28:56,720
I'm back.

294
00:29:00,160 --> 00:29:02,839
This is for you, Dad.
And sweet drink for you, Mom.

295
00:29:02,840 --> 00:29:05,000
- Thank you.
- Here.

296
00:29:18,440 --> 00:29:19,400
Da.

297
00:29:28,000 --> 00:29:29,840
I feel so sorry for Win.

298
00:29:31,880 --> 00:29:34,080
Why did he have to die like this?

299
00:29:38,200 --> 00:29:40,080
It's each person's karma.

300
00:29:41,280 --> 00:29:42,680
I want you to come to terms with it,

301
00:29:43,880 --> 00:29:47,880
because no matter what,
we can't help Mr. Prawin anymore.

302
00:29:55,760 --> 00:29:57,000
I don't have anyone left.

303
00:29:59,080 --> 00:30:02,120
Dad, Mom,

304
00:30:04,120 --> 00:30:05,200
and now Win.

305
00:30:06,760 --> 00:30:08,280
Everyone has left me.

306
00:30:21,080 --> 00:30:22,560
Who said you have no one?

307
00:30:23,080 --> 00:30:24,720
You still have me.

308
00:30:27,640 --> 00:30:29,280
I'll take care of you.

309
00:30:41,960 --> 00:30:45,640
Da, marry me.

310
00:31:09,400 --> 00:31:10,440
Will you?

311
00:31:44,200 --> 00:31:46,480
Na, don't speak loudly.

312
00:31:49,520 --> 00:31:50,920
What is Mr. Thongdee doing?

313
00:31:52,320 --> 00:31:56,120
He's trying to find a way
to get Win's spirit off the island.

314
00:31:58,480 --> 00:32:01,360
He needs silence.

315
00:32:02,240 --> 00:32:03,719
He said do not call him,

316
00:32:03,720 --> 00:32:05,360
make a loud noise

317
00:32:06,480 --> 00:32:09,440
or touch him before he opens his eyes.

318
00:32:14,640 --> 00:32:15,880
Astral projection.

319
00:32:17,720 --> 00:32:18,800
What?

320
00:32:21,360 --> 00:32:23,800
He must be astral projecting
to Skull Island.

321
00:32:25,200 --> 00:32:27,719
While his spirit is away from his body,

322
00:32:27,720 --> 00:32:30,719
no one must call him or touch him.

323
00:32:30,720 --> 00:32:33,080
Or his spirit may not be able to return.

324
00:33:02,280 --> 00:33:03,480
So this is Skull Island?

325
00:33:04,160 --> 00:33:06,640
It's as quiet as a deserted island.

326
00:33:08,520 --> 00:33:09,760
Of course, it's quiet.

327
00:33:10,600 --> 00:33:13,319
The police sealed it off.

328
00:33:13,320 --> 00:33:15,119
No one can enter the island.

329
00:33:15,120 --> 00:33:18,080
Good. That makes things easier.

330
00:33:19,240 --> 00:33:21,160
Let's look for the gold
before it gets dark.

331
00:33:47,680 --> 00:33:48,720
What's wrong?

332
00:33:54,040 --> 00:33:55,920
Nothing.

333
00:33:57,080 --> 00:33:58,320
Let's go.

334
00:34:07,360 --> 00:34:09,199
Why aren't they scared of us?

335
00:34:11,239 --> 00:34:12,280
Exactly.

336
00:34:12,840 --> 00:34:14,719
They act like they can't even see us.

337
00:34:17,800 --> 00:34:19,320
Then how are we supposed to kill them?

338
00:34:55,920 --> 00:34:56,800
What is it?

339
00:34:57,320 --> 00:35:00,200
I feel strange,
like someone is following us.

340
00:35:06,600 --> 00:35:07,600
There's no one.

341
00:35:08,920 --> 00:35:10,520
But I really felt it.

342
00:35:11,080 --> 00:35:14,400
Felt like someone is following us
and watching us the whole time.

343
00:35:16,880 --> 00:35:17,759
Hey,

344
00:35:17,760 --> 00:35:19,359
can you stop freaking me out?

345
00:35:19,360 --> 00:35:21,720
You said this island didn't have ghosts.

346
00:35:24,720 --> 00:35:28,080
I'm probably just imagining things.
Let's hurry and find the gold.

347
00:35:35,720 --> 00:35:37,400
Why won't you let us kill them?

348
00:35:38,600 --> 00:35:40,960
That is not your duty.

349
00:35:43,240 --> 00:35:45,000
But they're here to take the gold.

350
00:35:48,000 --> 00:35:50,560
There is no way they can take the gold.

351
00:35:51,880 --> 00:35:56,200
Both of them share karmic ties
with Pat and Prawin.

352
00:35:57,800 --> 00:35:59,400
It has nothing to do with us.

353
00:36:06,480 --> 00:36:08,200
An intruder.

354
00:36:32,360 --> 00:36:35,280
You're very brave to come back here.

355
00:36:46,360 --> 00:36:48,120
I never came here to hurt anyone.

356
00:36:49,120 --> 00:36:51,640
You know you cannot defeat me.

357
00:36:53,080 --> 00:36:54,440
Even if we cannot defeat you,

358
00:36:55,080 --> 00:36:59,080
we will not simply stand by. Take him.

359
00:37:24,960 --> 00:37:27,560
That's Dad and Mom.
Na, what are we going to do?

360
00:37:29,320 --> 00:37:32,399
If Mr. Mek comes in now,
this will be a mess.

361
00:37:32,400 --> 00:37:37,119
Mook, Da, and I
will go out and intercept Dad first.

362
00:37:37,120 --> 00:37:40,319
Mr. Narathon, you stay inside here.

363
00:37:40,320 --> 00:37:41,840
Let's go.

364
00:37:53,360 --> 00:37:56,519
That's Na's car.
Why didn't he tell us he came here?

365
00:37:56,520 --> 00:38:00,040
He's a grown man now.
Let him do his thing.

366
00:38:03,640 --> 00:38:04,560
Dad.

367
00:38:05,360 --> 00:38:08,320
Na, why didn't you tell us you were
coming? We could've come together.

368
00:38:10,560 --> 00:38:12,319
Well, we didn't plan to come here, Dad.

369
00:38:12,320 --> 00:38:15,280
We were going somewhere else,
but we happened to pass by.

370
00:38:15,880 --> 00:38:17,040
What about you, Dad?

371
00:38:17,880 --> 00:38:21,040
I brought your mom to see Venerable Sir
about hosting the Kathin ceremony.

372
00:38:21,560 --> 00:38:24,000
But he has already left the monkhood.

373
00:38:24,600 --> 00:38:26,679
That's strange.
He's been ordained for a long time.

374
00:38:26,680 --> 00:38:29,000
Why would he leave without telling anyone?

375
00:38:32,960 --> 00:38:36,199
Mom, we were just about to go out
for something to eat.

376
00:38:36,200 --> 00:38:38,079
Come with us.

377
00:38:38,080 --> 00:38:41,799
That sounds good. I'm hungry too.

378
00:38:41,800 --> 00:38:45,120
I don't feel like cooking.
Eating out sounds nice, doesn't it?

379
00:38:46,360 --> 00:38:48,960
Shall we go now?

380
00:38:50,120 --> 00:38:52,079
Let's go.

381
00:38:52,080 --> 00:38:53,280
Hold on.

382
00:39:03,200 --> 00:39:05,920
What? What's going on?

383
00:39:30,560 --> 00:39:31,639
Venerable Sir.

384
00:39:31,640 --> 00:39:32,760
Dad.

385
00:39:34,360 --> 00:39:36,040
Let's talk outside, Dad.

386
00:39:38,440 --> 00:39:39,880
Why is he here?

387
00:39:40,600 --> 00:39:42,639
Don't speak loudly.

388
00:39:42,640 --> 00:39:44,799
Mr. Thongdee is astral projecting.

389
00:39:44,800 --> 00:39:47,039
If his concentration is disturbed,

390
00:39:47,040 --> 00:39:49,440
it could be dangerous.

391
00:40:01,520 --> 00:40:02,840
I'm back.

392
00:40:18,360 --> 00:40:20,120
What is going on, Venerable Sir.

393
00:40:22,920 --> 00:40:24,120
I mean, Mr. Thongdee?

394
00:40:44,840 --> 00:40:45,840
You can't go on anymore?

395
00:40:47,240 --> 00:40:49,639
I've never walked this far in my life.

396
00:40:49,640 --> 00:40:50,920
Let me rest for a moment.

397
00:40:55,640 --> 00:40:59,720
Hurry up. It's almost dark.
We don't have much time.

398
00:41:07,160 --> 00:41:08,960
How long do we have to
keep following these two?

399
00:41:10,120 --> 00:41:13,640
They don't seem like
they can see us at all.

400
00:41:15,360 --> 00:41:17,199
I don't know.

401
00:41:17,200 --> 00:41:21,000
But what I do know is,
if we want to leave this island,

402
00:41:21,640 --> 00:41:22,960
we have to kill them.

403
00:41:29,640 --> 00:41:32,600
Why does my life
have to be this miserable?

404
00:41:36,560 --> 00:41:37,960
And who are you?

405
00:41:38,920 --> 00:41:40,480
I'm Mr. Phum's wife.

406
00:41:41,080 --> 00:41:42,120
Wife?

407
00:41:43,400 --> 00:41:45,360
Someone like you?

408
00:41:46,320 --> 00:41:49,760
You could be his mistress at best.

409
00:41:54,880 --> 00:41:56,080
It's you.

410
00:42:02,280 --> 00:42:03,640
You know her?

411
00:42:05,240 --> 00:42:08,240
Of course. I know her very well.

412
00:42:09,600 --> 00:42:10,920
Sairung.

413
00:42:22,120 --> 00:42:23,120
What now?

414
00:42:24,960 --> 00:42:28,200
I heard something again,
like someone calling my name.

415
00:42:30,640 --> 00:42:32,959
Can you stop saying
and doing things like this?

416
00:42:32,960 --> 00:42:34,440
I'm already scared enough.

417
00:42:35,440 --> 00:42:36,800
What are you scared of?

418
00:42:37,480 --> 00:42:39,079
We've been on this island for ages.

419
00:42:39,080 --> 00:42:42,080
If there were ghosts,
they would've come out.

420
00:42:47,440 --> 00:42:48,480
Let's go.

421
00:42:49,280 --> 00:42:50,320
Sairung.

422
00:43:09,640 --> 00:43:13,120
You have to be my substitute.

423
00:43:14,480 --> 00:43:16,080
Everyone will die.

424
00:43:18,120 --> 00:43:20,000
- Thank you for dropping me off.
- No problem.

425
00:43:22,440 --> 00:43:24,480
I am the one you love.

426
00:43:25,120 --> 00:43:27,919
We will go together.

427
00:43:27,920 --> 00:43:29,239
Let me kill you.

428
00:43:29,240 --> 00:43:31,720
Then you can become my substitute.

429
00:44:04,160 --> 00:44:06,400
Subtitle translation by: Panuwat Baikeawon
